        "date": "2026-11-12T00:24:54Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): a Z pick with a Y pick keeps Z on Z in the WCS-from-features law\n\nThe (Z, Y) arm of align_roles was a copy of (Y, X): the Z pick's axis\nlanded in the Y slot and the squared Y pick in X, so a side face picked\nas Z with its edge as Y set a WCS lying on its back. Z now stays Z, the\nY pick is squared to it, and X = Y x Z closes the frame.\n\nPinned by mcp_wcs_features::set_wcs_from_features_lands_on_the_guis_frame_as_one_undo_step.\n\nRefs #937\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
